<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortĭfĭco</span></b> , 1,
			v. a.
		mortificus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to kill, destroy</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caro mortificatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 37</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to mortify, subject, reduce to weakness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Col. 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facta carnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rom. 8, 13</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7, 4</span></i>.</div>
